From adeb5417db2499a9f005296fc8f8ec5b4c4eff22 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rob Currie <rob@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 05:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] feat: a tree branch of whole TRef objects, as tref_test.C
 writes one

TTree::Branch("Refs", "TRef", &ref, 4000, 0) asks for the reference unsplit,
and it was refused for want of a layout. ROOT writes each entry as TRef's own
streamer does - a version, the number, the bits, the index of the file's
process record - which tref_record already made for a split collection, and
the file describes TRef by its TObject base alone.

- pyroot/trees/objects.py: WholeReference (a StreamedColumn of those records,
  with TRef described as wclasses.TREF says, the class carried rather than
  looked up among INFOS, which has no TRef) and Reference (the kind that
  writes one record an entry, and the file's ProcessID record for it). A
  split object branch's fBits now carries the heap's bits, as ROOT writes
  them - 0x3000008 where it wrote 0x8.

roottest/root/io/tree: tref-write UNSUPPORTED -> PASS, tref-read
UNSUPPORTED -> DIFF, 11 PASS / 0 FAIL / 9 DIFF / 0 UNSUPPORTED. tref-read
still prints bits: 0: reading a split branch of a bare TObject does not fill
the object (its member leaves are named fUniqueID/fBits, as ROOT names them,
and nothing resolves them to the branch's object).

tests: the refusal test now uses TNamed, and the new branch has a test of its
own (tests/test_pyroot_trees_objects_more.py).
